<<~ ahu #/meme-header>>

! Lararium Node — Quine-Wiki-Agentic-HUD Principles

This locus locks basic law for a self-describing, self-editing, self-projecting wiki-agent HUD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ observe that a quine-like wiki-agent can confuse its rendered surface with its authority membrane.
⏿ orient around canon carriers, visible origins, receipts, local-first stores, and projection boundaries.
◇ decide that every live surface may propose, render, and stage, but only an explicit authority ceremony may promote canon.
▶ act by preserving round trips, queueing projection writes, stamping origins, and refusing silent semantic loss.
⤴ assess boot, sync, projection, and promotion through receipts rather than vibes.
↺ hand off any unresolved drift as named residue before the next loop.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/authority-law>>

!! Authority Law

# ''Carrier canon first.'' Hostless `lar:///` carriers under `lares/` carry canon.
# ''Projection never promotes itself.'' TW5, tldraw, HUD, MCP, DreamDeck, and future Kowloon surfaces render and draft; they do not silently promote.
# ''Fork before overwrite.'' Live/session material may fork, annotate, propose, and request merge; it must not silently override invariant loci.
# ''Ceremony marks canon MOVE.'' Agentic or operator writes that reach `lares/` need actor, origin, target URI, diff, receipt, and rollback path.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/round-trip-law>>

!! Round-Trip Law

# ''Round-trip or refuse.'' Any carrier → tiddler/widget/shape → carrier path must preserve law-bearing structure or emit explicit loss residue.
# ''Small semantic chunks keep stable addresses.'' Ahu slots, anchors, fields, and edges need durable identity.
# ''Metadata counts as body law.'' Stripped display metadata must remain available for write-back.
# ''Regex may assist, not rule.'' Parser-backed spans should replace regex membranes where loss pressure grows.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/local-first-law>>

!! Local-First Law

# The operator can boot, inspect, edit, and recover locally.
# Network sync serves local agency; it does not define truth by itself.
# Every mutation carries visible origin: `canon-hydrate`, `tw-local`, `crdt-remote`, `canvas-draft`, `operator-import`, or another explicit class.
# Queue at projection boundaries where many live events target one artifact.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/receipt-law>>

!! Receipt Law

# Boot, promote, reseed, sync epoch, and projection batches should carry receipt lineage.
# Debug HUD state should agree with server authority state.
# Hashes exclude unstable timestamps unless the timestamp itself forms the claimed artifact.
# Missing or empty receipt state counts as visible boot residue.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/package-boundaries>>

!! Package Boundaries

```text
@lararium/mesh      no fs, no DOM, no TW5, no tldraw
@lararium/tw5       tiddler VM + filters + sync adaptor
@lararium/app       browser HUD/projection
@lararium/node      file, server, authority, receipt, promotion
lares/              canon membrane
```

Canonical flow:

```text
carrier canon
  → parser / graph / receipt
    → Automerge live store
      ↔ TW5 semantic/filter/edit VM
      → tldraw / HUD / DreamDeck projections
      → disk projector queue
        → carrier write-back only through explicit projection law or MOVE (residency ACTION)
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/red-flags>>

!! Red Flags

* Projection cache starts to look canonical.
* Child tiddler edits lose carrier metadata.
* Debounce drops sibling ahu edits.
* Agent writes without origin or receipt.
* Browser debug state disagrees with server receipt.
* Parser accepts malformed law silently.
* Convenient direct write bypasses ceremony.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

